  "theorem": {
    "statement": "On the canonical S^2 coexact carrier, if the physical boundary field is the coexact 1-form Ashtekar-Barbero connection and the canonical extension is a centered SO(3)-invariant one-loop Gaussian extension, then primitive line-transport dimensionality forces the spectral scale s = sqrt(r_s^2 Delta_1^coex), the one-loop per-mode generator is w_ell = log s_ell = (1/2) log lambda_ell, and a covariance payload alpha acts by the inverse Gaussian kernel N = exp(-alpha w) = s^(-alpha) = lambda^(-alpha/2).",
    "coefficient_fixing": "With alpha = K_gauge/x from the proved covariance readout and proved line-scale divisor, one gets N_ell proportional to lambda_ell^(-K_gauge/(2x))."
  },
  "claim_boundary": {
    "derived": [
      "For a coexact 1-form field, primitive line-transport dimensionality fixes the shell generator to w_ell = log sqrt(lambda_ell) = (1/2) log lambda_ell.",
      "A centered invariant one-loop Gaussian extension acts by the inverse kernel N = exp(-alpha w).",
      "With alpha = K_gauge/x this gives the Paper 28 determinant shell law N_ell proportional to lambda_ell^(-K_gauge/(2x))."
    ],
    "conditional": [
      "The physical A-vacuum canonical extension is indeed a centered SO(3)-invariant one-loop Gaussian extension of the coexact 1-form field."
    ]
  },
